The Ventas portfolio also includes outpatient medical buildings, research centers and healthcare facilities. Ventas, Inc. is based in Illinois, Chicago. Ventas, Inc. was incorporated in 1983 in Maryland.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Debra A. Cafaro J.D. | Chairman & CEO | Age 67 | Compensation: $5.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 542 people. Revenue per employee of $10.8M ranks in the top quartile among Real Estate peers, improving at 12%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $71K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Ventas, Inc. is a large-cap real estate business with a $46.9B market cap on $5.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +12% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 1% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $1.3B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 3.2% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 975% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":9.748002349710696},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 9% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["26 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Ventas (VTR) Lifts 2026 Outlook As Senior Housing Growth Puts Valuation Back In Focus","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nyse-vtr/ventas/news/ventas-vtr-lifts-2026-outlook-as-senior-housing-growth-puts","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793961034.446,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.807,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"How Ventas Inc. (VTR) Affects Rotational Strategy Timing","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/1/How_Ventas_Inc._VTR_Affects_Rotational_Strategy_Timing_11042607220