ar).","The sector is fragmented and competitive (HHI 0.03 across 145 companies in the universe; the top four hold 25% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares have drifted higher, up 12% over the past year excluding the latest month.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 13% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 23% and a beta of 0.62, it is more defensive than the market, though its beta has shifted (1y -0.27 vs 5y 0.54), so read it loosely.","Liquidity is deep, with about $271.2M traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 73% in the 2020 crash, 42% in the 2022 bear market and 64% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its blended-model fair value of $8.26 (margin of safety -975%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 88%), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Real Estate peers: P/E 170.7 vs 23.6 and EV/EBITDA 24.4 vs 16.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 31% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of -2.7% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 1.4% (vs the 8% bar).","The 22 covering analysts target $99.00 on average, 12% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 1% falls short of the cost of capital of 7.2%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.49).","It burns cash (FCF margin -22%).","AFFO margin (a proxy for distributable REIT cash) is -22%.","ROE of 2% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.2x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.7% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 5.6x net debt to EBITDA ($741.1M of cash against $13.0B of debt), and interest cover is thin at 1.3x.","The value-trap profile is elevated (50/100); see the breakdown below."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 12.2% over 3 years, 9.0% over 5 years and 5.9% over 10 years, so growth is accelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 22%).","At current returns, reinvesting 100% of profits supports about 1.3% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","Forward indicators: FFO growth of 2.6% a year over five years.","Capex runs 2.1x depreciation (50.2% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is -14, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.5%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Net share issuance leaves shareholder yield negative (-3.2%), diluting holders.","The share count has grown 4.0% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","It pays out 392% of earnings, more than it earns, so the dividend is at risk."],"people":["With about 542 employees, each generates about $10.8M of revenue, 4.7x the Real Estate median, and productivity has risen 12.1% a year.","Free cash flow is negative, at -$2.4M per employee.","CEO pay is $5.5M (1x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $71K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":18,"head":"Avoid: priced 975% above its fair value of $8.26.","pros":["Revenue grew 9.0%/yr over 5y","12-1 month momentum +12%"],"cons":["Model rating PASS (composite 22, gates 4/25)","Trades 975% above fair value of $8.26","ROIC 1.3% vs WACC 7.2%","FCF margin 22.0% (burns cash)","Net debt/EBITDA 5.6x"],"flags":["Priced 975% above its fair value of $8.26","Earns below its cost of capital and burns cash","Operating income covers interest only 1.3x","The model rates it PASS"],"need":[],"buy_below":7.02,"vc":{"base":8.26,"base_src":"blend","bear":null,"bull":null,"alt_median":8.26,"n_alt":3,"gap":null,"dispersion":0.8778,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (88% dispersion)"]},"med":{"pe":23.5593,"ev_ebitda":16.316,"pfcf":17.832,"pb":1.3568,"roic":0.0411,"gross_margin":0.5765,"fcf_margin":0